                <pb facs="0248" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to. Mr. Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports the unconditional surrender of the insurgents which took
                    place thirty minutes after the city batteries opened fire and without a shot
                    being fired from their side. It is believed that Da Gama has taken refuge on a
                    Portuguese war vessel.</p>
            </div>
